    73	4. **The forward sham rule (per-author condition)** on the planting's sham regime: attributable = plants with any planted author flagged among the delivered sham plants none of whose planted authors is flagged on honest pairs alone (the author's maximum over all their honest dossier pairs in the same judge and reading, the target document's pair included), one-sided 95 percent lower bound = the two-sided 90 percent Clopper-Pearson lower end; *not interpretable* when the bound exceeds 0.10, *interpretable, with caution* when only the point does, *interpretable* otherwise; a label only on a full control of at least 64 plants, every one scored (`stage3_t1replant_score.forward_sham_rule`'s per-author half, unchanged). v3's 32-plant control takes no label; the B0 weak-link sensitivity (the 32-plant attributable lower bound at or under 0.10) is reported beside.
