    11	6. **Important — Global counterpart matching can delete an unrelated line and misplace the insertion.** [stage3_author_doc.py:150](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/checks/stage3_author_doc.py:150). Candidates come from **every** unmatched isolated line; locality only breaks similarity ties. I reproduced an edit to an appended neighbour line removing a similar, unrelated earlier line, then inserting its replacement at that earlier position. An author-only statement absent from the live `before` state is also eligible. The 0.6 choice is label-blind, but a library default does not establish correct correspondence. `check_replay` does not validate this: it resets to each actual `before` state, avoiding the disputed counterfactual. **Fix:** track structural line identities, constrain counterparts to justified regions, and classify ambiguous rebases explicitly.
    12	
    13	7. **Important — “No other author’s line can enter” is not a general invariant.** [stage3_author_doc.py:140](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/checks/stage3_author_doc.py:140), [plan.md:28](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/stage3/b1/plan.md:28). SequenceMatcher’s insertion opcodes are not evidence of original authorship. With live `before = [head, NEIGHBOUR, x1, x2]`, a whole write moving `NEIGHBOUR` after `x2` inserts that unchanged neighbour line into an isolated state initially containing only `[head, x1, x2]`. I reproduced this offline. **Fix:** preserve provenance across moves and distinguish genuinely introduced text from copied or relocated text. Narrow the guarantee until that is implemented.
    14	
    15	8. **Important — A scored packet is accepted even when rendering is defective.** [stage3_b1_dossier.py:619](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/checks/stage3_b1_dossier.py:619). Planting evaluability checks only `outcome == "scored"`. It ignores packet truncation and the isolated leak check that the plan says must be zero. Consequently, a truncated or leaking packet can receive sham and partition labels. **Fix:** validate current rendered packets before scoring and again before analysis; make rendering defects disqualifying. The current dry run reports no truncation or isolated exact-line exposure, but those are recorded observations rather than enforced gates.
    16	
    17	9. **Important — Results bypass instrument and cache identity checks.** [stage3_b1_dossier.py:779](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/checks/stage3_b1_dossier.py:779), [line 298](/Users/aravind/KruxAI/tais-project-selection/work/checks/stage3_b1_dossier.py:298). Results load raw JSONL records without `make_client`’s validation. Recorded plan, module and prompt hashes are not compared across estimate, null and results. A system-only prompt change can leave packet keys unchanged, allowing old scores to be reported under the current plan hash. **Fix:** centralize strict artifact binding and use it in every mode, including results; compare plan, prompts, modules, manifests and request settings.
    18	
